  str_n28_15_name = "ST4 - Punishment",
  str_n28_1_name_desc = "/",
  str_n28_2_name_desc = "A case about a decapitated statue is placed in your charge, however, the plaintiff's claim is not damage to public property, but... obstruction of love?",
  str_n28_3_name_desc = "In this season, when the ardor of Mooncrown Day still lingers in the air, Tina has her own desires to pursue.",
  str_n28_4_name_desc = "Go and experience the legendary Moonlight Salon, immerse yourself in the amorous atmosphere, and uncover the truth!",
  str_n28_5_name_desc = "/",
  str_n28_6_name_desc = "It is only when Schwab's embarrassment becomes evident that you realize the terrible misunderstanding that has occurred.",
  str_n28_7_name_desc = "You find the organizer of the salon, an ordinary nun from Lumopolis, but receive some unexpected answers.",
  str_n28_8_name_desc = "/",
  str_n28_9_name_desc = "Eclipsites, at a time like this? They really are such strange creatures...",
  str_n28_10_name_desc = "As the Eclipsite threat gradually approaches the statue, don't forget to protect the statue in the battle!",
  str_n28_11_name_desc = "Get rid of the pursuers on your tail and get ready to fight without any restriction!",
  str_n28_12_name_desc = "Are the basements of all nobles filled with so much muck!?",
  str_n28_13_name_desc = "Don't let the smallest detail slide without scrutiny—reveal the truth behind the case in the Hall of Justice!",
  str_n28_14_name_desc = "The court is under Schwab's absolute control! There is no longer any chance for justice to prevail here. We must find a way out of this first, then think of another way!",
  str_n28_15_name_desc = "/",
  str_n28_1_name_desc_long = "After the end of the Mooncrown Day festival, the lingering charm of amour still floats through the streets of Lumopolis. A lovestruck couple comes to the Hall of Justice and makes a scene. The case even catches Schwartz's attention, who happens to be present for an inspection. In the face of the upcoming structural changes to the Hall of Justice, several young judges exhibit different reactions—Leyn continues working obliviously, Matthieu invites you and Carleen to share in an interesting occurrence, and Tina, who is always so cheerful, seems to have her own worries.",
  str_n28_2_name_desc_long = "The Romance Division's first case that no one is willing to deal with is placed in your hands. A statue has been decapitated and the plaintiff insists that the lifeless statue is his lover. You go to where the Hall of Justice keeps case exhibits and inspect the statue for clues. Outside the window, a \"moon\" quietly rises.",
  str_n28_3_name_desc_long = "With no apparent clues to follow up, Tina invites you to visit her home. It turns out that she has been troubled by something for quite some time and hopes you can help her plan of meeting him come to fruition. You immediately understand from Tina's words that she is secretly in love with your new boss, Schwab.",
  str_n28_4_name_desc_long = "You decide to go to the Moonlight Salon to try your luck and see if you can find the object of Tina's affection. Tina also brings a gift she intends to give to. At the salon, you dance, chat, and enjoy the festive songs, but the city guard suddenly shatters this blissful moment. The guards are hell-bent on suppressing this private gathering, and amid the chaos, another statue is broken, and Tina's gift is lost.",
  str_n28_5_name_desc_long = "You immediately head to the Hall of Justice to report the matter, but run into another pair of lovers determined to enter into a heated legal battle. The two of them were in fact present at the salon... It turns out that Tina's lost gift caused a misunderstanding between them, and although Tina rushes in to explain the situation, the matter takes an unexpected turn...",
  str_n28_6_name_desc_long = "Because of Tina's testimony in court, Schwab ends up being embarrassed in front of everyone. After leaving the Hall of Justice, you realize that you were too quick to guess who Tina's crush was, based on her explanation. The gift was never meant for Schwab, but was in fact meant for the little Eclipsite who seems to show up everywhere—Toto.",
  str_n28_7_name_desc_long = "Before you prepare to leave, Loewe suddenly brings some new insight to Carleen in the form of new information. It appears that every time the Moonlight Salon is held, riots break out, and the heads of statues mysteriously disappear. In light of this breakthrough, the organizer of the Moonlight Salon seems very suspicious in your eyes, but when you meet the organizer again, your suspicions are instantly dispelled.",
  str_n28_8_name_desc_long = "Byron, the plaintiff in the decapitated statue case, comes to the Hall of Justice to file a complaint and asks to see the investigation results as soon as possible. Fresh out of clues, the judges replace the statue's severed head in the act of desperation. Of course, Byron is not amused by such a careless gesture, but he does not have the time to stay angry—his beloved \"statue wife\" is in peril. The judges immediately rush to the Stairway to the Skies, where a parade is about to be held.",
  str_n28_9_name_desc_long = "The statue requiring protection is at the top of the stairway, in the direction of the advancing procession. In order to rescue the statue from being destroyed in the chaos, the judges try to stop the parade through unconventional means. Just as you are about to succeed, Eclipsites begin rampaging at the parade's rear, and the crowd flees toward the stairway.",
  str_n28_10_name_desc_long = "You try to keep the statue safe. Eclipsites close in from behind the crowd, and panic surrounds. In the chaos of battle, a shadowy hand reaches out from the darkness and breaks off the head of the statue, but at least Leyn manages to pull a glove off the unknown culprit's hand. The heartbroken Byron returns to the Hall of Justice, while Schwab seems sure that he has the case wrapped up, ordering Tina's arrest.",
  str_n28_11_name_desc_long = "The glove obtained by Leyn becomes the key evidence pointing to Tina's guilt, and Schwab arrests her. You firmly believe that Tina is innocent and cannot ignore Schwab's strange behavior, as it seems as though he is framing her. Perhaps if you can find out his motives, you can exonerate Tina. Leyn decides to take a risk and sneaks into Schwab's house to have a look around.",
  str_n28_12_name_desc_long = "You sneak into Schwab's house to observe him. Although Schwab's behavior is somewhat strange, there is nothing particularly suspicious about him. You open the passage to Schwab's basement by chance, and a swarm of Eclipsites emerges from it. You flee Schwab's home in a panic—time is running out, as the day of the trial approaches.",
  str_n28_13_name_desc_long = "The trial of the \"Serial Statue Decapitations\" finally begins. Leyn and Matthieu insist that Tina is innocent, and after a fierce defense, Leyn pounces upon the contradiction between the glove and Tina's hand, successfully clearing her name. However, this matter is far from over. Leyn invites a special witness to take the stand. Toto has come to the witness stand, ready to prove that the true culprit is Schwab.",
  str_n28_14_name_desc_long = "Toto and Leyn planned out an ingenious strategy in advance, whereby Toto pretended to be the culprit responsible for vandalizing the statues,　successfully bringing Schwab's plot to light. In his desperation, Schwab reveals his trump card—he has replaced the jury members with Eclipsites! His verdict has nothing to do with the truth. You escape from the Hall of Justice, but are confronted by the deranged Schwab at the gate. In the end, you succeed in subduing him. The case ends with the bursting of the moon balloon—it seems as though the wave of romance filling the air will fade along with it.",
  str_n28_15_name_desc_long = "Irridon tries the case again and convicts the guilty party. This farce was fairly harmless, so Schwab would not be imprisoned. Although for him, the punishment he receives may be even more unbearable than imprisonment. You and the judges also receive a token punishment for your unorthodox behavior. After receiving the gift from Tina, Toto is ready to embark on a new journey; his departure makes you look forward to the next time you meet. As hymns float in the air, Lumopolis returns to how it once was.",
  str_n28_h1_name = "H1 - Onslaught",
  str_n28_h2_name = "H2 - Deathly Din",
  str_n28_h3_name = "H3 - Resolve",
  str_n28_h4_name = "H4 - The Chase",
  str_n28_h5_name = "H5 - Unyielding",
  str_n28_h6_name = "H6 - The Cavalry",
  str_n28_h7_name = "EX1 - Strive to Survive",
  str_n28_h8_name = "EX2 - Searing Lightning",
  str_n28_h9_name = "EX3 - Bladed Shadows",
  str_n28_h10_name = "EX4 - Swarm",
  str_n28_h11_name = "EX5 - Blood Rage",
  str_n28_h12_name = "EX 6 - Central Strike",
  str_n28_h1_name_desc = "The enemies are elusive and move around quickly, but the most frightening thing is that they're willing to sacrifice their lives to defeat you.",
  str_n28_h2_name_desc = "Rumbling thunders fill the air. When they fall, perhaps you can use their powerful blasts to attack the enemies.",
  str_n28_h3_name_desc = "Although the enemy is overwhelming, with the help of your allies, you just might be able to turn the tide.",
  str_n28_h4_name_desc = "The terrain is tricky and your foes are many—simply making it out alive would be a miracle. Watch out for the enemies chasing after you!",
  str_n28_h5_name_desc = "Besieged by countless enemies, how can you carve out a bloody path to salvation? What's more, once these enemies die, they become stronger and stronger...",
  str_n28_h6_name_desc = "They look like Lumo Knights, but under their stone masks lie vicious Eclipsites. You cannot afford to fall!",
  str_n28_h7_name_desc = "Your pursuers are getting closer... How will your allies manage to survive?",
  str_n28_h8_name_desc = "Flames and echoing blasts surround... The enemy seems unbeatable, but time will become the key to your victory.",
  str_n28_h9_name_desc = "Shadows lurk in every corner, and sharp blades seek your flesh at every turn. A hard battle lies ahead of you.",
  str_n28_h10_name_desc = "The endless inundation of enemies forms a seething swarm, flooding from the nest in the central area...",
  str_n28_h11_name_desc = "The enemy's blades are as sharp as the biting wind, and their attacks are deadlier than a raging gale. More terrifying than this is the fact that once they are intoxicated by the smell of blood, they become even stronger...",
  str_n28_h12_name_desc = "Although you're not absolutely certain, the enemy standing at the center of the battlefield may harbor hidden intentions...",
